   "provider": "Dr. Mary Hughes",
   "specialty": "pulmonology",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - West LLC Medical Group**\n\n**Patient:** Randy Schmidt \n**DOB:** 08/25/1967 \n**Sex:** M \n**MRN:** 858539\n\n**Encounters:**\n\n- **2026-03-19:** Back strain \n - **BP:** 117/82 \n - **Weight:** 210 lbs \n\n- **2025-05-25:** COPD \n - **BP:** 116/75 \n - **Weight:** lbs \n\n- **2024-07-31:** Ankle sprain \n - **BP:** 111/80 \n - **Weight:** 211 lbs \n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:**\n\n- **Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD):**\n - Randy Schmidt has been diagnosed with COPD, with the onset of symptoms noted April 23, 2015. Currently, his condition is controlled. His FEV1 (Forced Expiratory Volume in 1 second) is at 94% of the predicted value. He does not require home oxygen therapy. His current medication regimen includes umeclidinium-vilanterol 62.5/25, which he takes as prescribed. The patient has been educated on importance of adherence and regular follow-up visits to monitor his condition.\n\n- **Back Strain:**\n - On March 19, 2026, Mr. Schmidt presented with complaints of back strain. Physical examination revealed tenderness in the lumbar region without any neurological deficits. Blood pressure was 117/82 mmHg, and his weight was 210 lbs. He was advised to engage in back-strengthening exercises, use ice/heat therapy, and take over-the-counter pain relievers as needed. He was also advised avoid heavy lifting and to practice good body mechanics to prevent further injury. A follow-up appointment was scheduled to assess his recovery.\n\n- **Ankle Sprain:**\n - On July 31, 2024, Mr. Schmidt came in with an ankle sprain. The physical exam revealed swelling and tenderness around the ankle joint, consistent with a grade 1 sprain. Blood pressure was 111/80 mmHg, and his weight was 211 lbs. He was instructed to use the RICE method (Rest, Ice, Elevation), avoid putting weight on the affected ankle, and use a supportive brace. He was also prescribed a short course of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) to manage pain and inflammation. He advised to return if symptoms worsened or did not improve within a few weeks.\n\n- **Social History:**\n - Mr. Schmidt has a history of tobacco use, specifically cigarettes, which he started on May 16, 1997. He smoked about half a pack per day but successfully quit on June 20, 1998. Currently, he has been tobacco-free for over 23 years. He reports consuming approximately six alcoholic drinks per week. His mother had a myocardial infarction at the age of 65 passed away at 76 years old.\n\n---\n\n**Vitals:**\n\n- **2026-03-19:** BP 117/82, Wt 210 lbs \n- **2025-05"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "-25:** BP 116/75, Wt 207 lbs \n- **2024-07-31:** BP 111/80, Wt 211 lbs \n\n---\n\n**General Physical Exam (Non-focal Findings):**\n\n- **Cardiovascular:** Normal heart sounds, no murmurs or gallops. \n- **Respiratory:** Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes or rales. \n- **Musculoskeletal:** No joint deformities, muscle strength 5/5 in all extremities. \n- **Neurological:** Alert and oriented x3, cranial nerves II-XII intact.\n\n---\n\n**Follow-Up:**\n\n- Mr. Schmidt is advised to continue his current COPD management plan and follow up in 3 months or sooner if symptoms worsen. He is also encouraged to maintain a healthy lifestyle, including regular physical activity within his limits, and avoid exposure to respiratory irritants. Further investigations or interventions will be considered based on his progress and any new symptoms that may arise.\n\n---\n\n**Signature:**\n\n**Dr. Mary Hughes, Pulmonologist** \nWest LLC Medical Group\n"
